Implement the backend part of **US-01-R1-F04 and F05**, per spec v0.4 §7.5 (Approved) and **ADR-0006** (Accepted 2026-11-21). Read both first. Branch `feat/us-01-data-form`: do not push or switch branches. The frontend-developer is updating the frontend parser to the same contract in parallel. **Do not run the full e2e suite**: it will fail until both sides are done, and the orchestrator runs the gate afterwards. Do not touch `frontend/`, `specs/` or tests. Do not start background commands.

1. **F04: typed rule attributes.** In `backend/src/components/form/validation-rule.json`:
   - `value` becomes `decimal` (replacing `json`);
   - add `pattern` (`string`);
   - keep `years`, `maxYearsOld`, `maxYearsAhead` (integers), `kind` and `message`.

   Update the seed (`backend/src/seed/`) so pattern rules carry their regex in `pattern` (with `value` null) and numeric kinds use a numeric `value`. Every rule exposes all its attributes, with the unused ones `null`, exactly as in §7.5.1. ADR-0006 says to reset the dev volume, because the idempotent seed does not rewrite existing rule rows. Make sure a fresh volume produces the right data. If you see a cheap, safe way for the seed to correct rule rows on an existing database, mention it; do not build anything elaborate.
2. **F05: expose `localeTag`.** Remove the custom `find` in `backend/src/api/country/controllers/country.ts` and go back to `createCoreController('api::country.country')`. The API then returns `localeTag` as stored. Keep the router's published-only config from 345a016 intact.

Verify on your own clean stack, backend only: `docker compose -p mci-be up -d --build --wait strapi`, then with anonymous curl on :1337:
- `GET /api/form-fields?filters[country][code][$eq]=CO&populate=*&sort=sortOrder:asc&pagination[pageSize]=100` returns rules in the §7.5.1 shape (show one pattern rule and one yearRange rule);
- `GET /api/countries?fields[0]=code&fields[1]=name&fields[2]=currencyCode&fields[3]=localeTag&fields[4]=sortOrder&sort=sortOrder:asc` returns `localeTag`;
- `sort=localeTag:asc` and `filters[localeTag][$eq]=es-CO` both return 200;
- the F01 checks still hold: `Authorization: foo` and `/API/` with `status=draft` return no drafts.

Then `docker compose -p mci-be down -v`. Also run `cd backend && npx tsc --noEmit && npm run lint && npm run build && npm test` (9/9; if the T-38 backend test depends on the rule shape and fails, report it with details, because the test-engineer owns it), and `bash scripts/scan-secrets.sh`.

Commit per finding (`fix(backend): …`, `Resolves: US-01-R1-F04` or `F05`, `Refs: ADR-0006, US-01-AC-14, US-01-AC-17`, Co-Authored-By trailer) with `git add <paths> && git commit … -- <paths>`. Never run `git add -A`.

Report: the commits, the curl evidence (the actual JSON snippets), and the command outputs.

